{
  "snapshot_date": "2026-08-17",
  "notes": "Prices in USD per 1M tokens, standard (non-batch) API tier. Tiered-price models record the base (lowest) tier with the higher tier in the model's note field. Retired models excluded; deprecated-but-available models included. Collected Monday on schedule. Tracked scope follows the set established on 2026-07-16 so week-over-week deltas stay meaningful: provider pages also list older or non-text models (OpenAI gpt-5.2 and earlier, Mistral Mixtral/NeMo/Ministral/Voxtral, Google image, embedding, TTS, video, and robotics models) that were outside scope then and remain outside it now. This week the tracked set moved for the first time since 2026-07-16, going from 46 rows to 43. Two models entered: Google's gemini-3.7-flash, released 2026-08-13, and xAI's grok-4.6. Five left: claude-opus-4-1 retired from the first-party API on 2026-08-05 (it remains available on Bedrock and Google Cloud, which this series does not track), and magistral-medium, magistral-small, devstral-2, and devstral-small-2 are absent from Mistral's pricing page, with the models overview giving retirement dates from 2025-10-31 through 2026-07-31. Those five were carried in earlier snapshots after their retirement dates had already passed; earlier files are left as collected rather than corrected. Three price moves: gemini-3.6-flash was cut in half to $0.75/$3.75 (cache $0.075), matching the 3.7 launch rate and carrying the same 2026-12-31 promotional expiry, and both DeepSeek models rose sharply — v4-flash off-peak input $0.14 to $0.22 and output $0.28 to $0.66, v4-pro input $0.435 to $0.66 and output $0.87 to $1.98 — which is the increase the 2026-08-10 notes flagged as expected but undated. DeepSeek also shipped a new pro build, V4-Pro-0813. Anthropic resolved a forward signal in the other direction: the Claude Sonnet 5 introductory $2/$10 is now the standard price and the 2026-09-01 increase to $3/$15 has been cancelled, so the 2026-09-07 snapshot should no longer be expected to show it. Observed but deliberately left out of the rows: Mistral now resells Z.ai GLM 5.2 (listed as zai-glm-5-2 on the pricing page and z-ai-glm-5-2 in the models overview) and lists Ministral 3 in three sizes; both sit outside the scope fixed on 2026-07-16 and are recorded here rather than added unilaterally. Anthropic's fast-mode premium ($10/$50 for Opus 5 and Opus 4.8) and 1.1x US data-residency multiplier remain request-time modifiers on the base rate rather than separate model rows, so they stay outside this schema.",
